course: dictionary
lesson: 14539
title: Words for people at work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can name a whole group of workers: personnel. It means the people who work for an organisation, such as an army, a hospital or a company. Another word for them is staff.
explain: Personnel is a group word, so it means all the workers together. «The hospital needs more medical personnel this winter.» The medical personnel are the doctors, nurses and others who care for patients.
explain: You will often see this word on doors and signs. «Authorised personnel only» means only staff who are allowed may go in. The sign is about safety, so read it carefully and obey it.
explain: Long ago, personnel could also mean the department that hires and looks after workers. Today that job is usually called Human Resources, or HR.
fact: Personnel means the people who work for an organisation. It is another word for staff.
fact: Personnel is a group word, so it means all the workers together.
fact: «Medical personnel» means the doctors, nurses and others who care for patients.
fact: «Military personnel» means the people who serve in an army.
fact: «Authorised personnel only» means only staff who are allowed may go in.
exercise: «Authorised personnel only» is written on a door. What does it mean? | The door is broken | Anyone can go in | *Only staff who are allowed may go in | Only children may go in
exercise: «The ship needed more medical personnel after the storm.» What does personnel mean here? | *The workers, such as the doctors and nurses | The ship's flags | The storm clouds | The ship's engines
exercise: Which word means about the same as personnel? | *staff | river | swimming | window
test: «The army sent military personnel to help the town.» Who are military personnel? | *Soldiers and others who serve in the army | People who sell food in the market | Animals on a farm | Teachers at a school
test: A ship has 120 personnel. They work in 3 equal shifts. How many personnel are in each shift? | *40 | 30 | 120 | 60
exam: Which sentence uses personnel correctly? | The personnel sang loudly in the rain. | I personnel my bedroom every Saturday. | The personnel of the cake was delicious. | *The hospital's personnel work in shifts to care for patients.
